  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "ChalkQL 0.6.1 makes long-running hosts leaner: execution arenas keep what their executions need, and standing views stop accumulating memory for rows they no longer hold.\n\n      - **Arenas:** `ExecutionArena.WorkingSetBytes` reports what a repeated execution needs retained to rent nothing from the heap. An arena now keeps its working set, with `ArenaOptions.WorkingSetMargin` (1% by default) as room, up to `RetainBytes`, which becomes a ceiling on memory rather than a measure of need. Arenas that need little hold little; a ceiling is all a host sets.\n      - **Managed output:** a projection's, filter's or join's batches are copied out of the arena at their exact size, so repeated statements stop rebuilding output in fresh heap arrays.\n      - **Standing views:** a maintained view whose state has mostly emptied rebuilds itself, and long-lived views hold far less spare room: stores grow by half rather than doubling, and key maps give memory back when they compact.\n      - **Compatibility:** additive API only. Arenas now retain less memory by default; set `RetainBytes` as the ceiling you want.\n\n      Full release notes:\n      https://github.com/markhammond/chalkql/releases/tag/v0.6.1",
